1. DEFINITIONS
“Buildora CMS” or “Software” means the proprietary Buildora CMS application, source code, documentation, and supplied files, excluding Third-Party Components. “Licensor” means the legal person identified above. “Buyer” means the person or entity that lawfully purchased this license. “Production Website” means the single live website serving its intended public or commercial purpose. “Production Domain” means its normalized registrable domain; the bare domain and its www subdomain (for example, example.com and www.example.com) are treated as one domain. “Non-Production Installation” means a copy used only for development, testing, backup, or deployment preparation. “End Client” means the one client receiving the completed Production Website. “Third-Party Components” means separately authored software or assets governed by their own notices or licenses. “Extended Support Add-on” means the optional support service described in section 10 and is not an extended software license.

2. ACCEPTANCE AND GRANT
Subject to payment, lawful acquisition, and compliance with this License, Licensor grants Buyer a limited, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable, and non-transferable license to install, use, and modify Buildora CMS for one Production Website on one Production Domain. The sole transfer exception is the completed-site handover in section 5. No ownership, copyright, trademark, patent, or other intellectual-property interest is sold.

3. SINGLE PRODUCTION DOMAIN
One license permits one Production Website on one Production Domain. Buyer must not reuse it for a second website, domain, client project, or independent commercial deployment. Redirects or aliases do not create permission for another website. A license permanently assigned to a completed website remains assigned to that website/domain even after handover; Buyer may not retain or recycle it for another project.

4. LOCAL AND STAGING RIGHTS
Buyer may maintain localhost, 127.0.0.1, ::1, local-development, .test, and .local installations, and one or more development/staging subdomains associated with the licensed Production Website. Each must be used only for development, testing, backup, or deployment preparation, must not operate as a separate public commercial website, and must not bypass the one-Production-Domain limit. These installations do not replace or change the production binding.

5. MODIFICATION AND END-CLIENT HANDOVER
Buyer may modify PHP, Laravel, Blade, CSS, JavaScript, and database-related application code; customize modules, layouts, branding, logos, colors, and frontend design; add private features; and integrate third-party services for the licensed website. Buyer may hand the modified application to one End Client solely as part of the completed licensed Production Website. The End Client takes the site subject to this License, and the license stays permanently assigned to it. Buyer must provide this License and applicable third-party notices and must not retain a reusable production copy.

6. PUBLIC-FACING WHITE-LABEL RIGHTS
Buyer may remove public “Powered by Buildora CMS” attribution; display Buyer or End Client names, logos, colors, and copyright text; brand the public website; and use supported company branding on the administrator login and ordinary admin interface. These presentation rights do not allow Buyer to claim authorship or ownership of Buildora CMS, remove source copyright notices, this License, or required third-party notices, falsify protected identity in System Information, rename and resell the Software, remove licensing for redistribution, or operate prohibited SaaS. Protected product identity may remain in System Information, license information and management, diagnostics, source headers, release manifests, and third-party notices.

7. PROHIBITED RESALE, DISCLOSURE, AND REDISTRIBUTION
Buyer must not sell, sublicense, rent, lease, share, give away, publish, or redistribute the original or modified Software as a CMS, template, source code, standalone product, marketplace item, public repository, or part of another downloadable software package. Buyer must not upload the full source to a public Git repository; create and sell a competing CMS based substantially on Buildora CMS; extract and redistribute major modules as another commercial product; bypass verification to facilitate redistribution; or use one license for multiple client websites. Sharing is limited to personnel and contractors who need access to build or operate the licensed website and are bound by confidentiality and use restrictions at least as protective as these terms, and to the permitted End Client handover.

